Attribution
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Baton is a derivative work of the "handoff" skill from metaswarm:

    metaswarm — Multi-agent orchestration framework for Claude Code,
                Gemini CLI, and Codex CLI
    Author:   Dave Sifry
    Source:   https://github.com/dsifry/metaswarm
    License:  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Dave Sifry

The document structure, method steps, template, and anti-patterns originate
from metaswarm's handoff skill and are used under the terms of the MIT License.

Baton's additions over the original:
  - Section 0 "Receiving Session Orchestration" — appoints the main agent as
    the session orchestrator following $efficient-frontier and declares review
    depth and boot sequence before any work begins.
  - Provider-neutral specialist and model routing for likely subagent lanes,
    including capability-aware reasoning effort, Claude and Codex model
    families, and same-runtime availability fallbacks.
  - Collision-aware deployment waves with launch triggers, disjoint ownership,
    single-writer boundaries, copy-ready packets, and independent review.
  - Optimal useful concurrency rather than blanket maximum fan-out.
  - Generalization to be framework-agnostic (no hard dependency on any
    orchestration framework, issue tracker, or plugin).

Grateful thanks to Dave Sifry and the metaswarm project.
